    {
      "id": "claim_565eaa338b6846008522b35d9b3b2202",
      "statement": "TypeScript is split across two project-reference files coordinated by the bare tsconfig.json: tsconfig.app.json (renderer, include src, types vite/client, JSX, DOM libs) and tsconfig.node.json (main/preload/build/e2e, types node). Both are noEmit: true and neither is composite, which lets pure modules like src/git/url.ts and src/git/relpath.ts be imported into electron/main.ts under the node program and reached by vitest's src/** include under the app program, typechecking identically in both.",
