    {
      "id": "claim_922dbe3ab48e46469c8a35be949aef5a",
      "statement": "On disk, a project stores only schema and paper metadata in project.json; every reviewer's and the consolidated annotation answers live in a sibling annotations/<paperId>/ folder, one file per reviewer plus a consolidated file. The split was introduced to avoid git-merge conflicts between reviewers editing the same all-in-one file; the model layer keeps the logical whole-project shape and ElectronAdapter.saveProject does the split, while the read side reassembles a split project back into that logical text before handing it to the renderer.",
